Design Sheet: "Floyd-Glass" TUI
Core Philosophy: Marry the atmospheric, pink-themed identity of FLOYD with the structured, professional layout of GEMINI. The UI should feel like a sleek, futuristic command center, not just a simple terminal.

1. Visual Hierarchy & Layout (Adopted from GEMINI)
Persistent Header: The PRISM_ART will be locked at the top, but it will be contained within its own distinct panel.
Zoned Main Content: The central area will be clearly divided into two main sections:
A scrollable Chat/Output Viewport.
A dedicated Error Notification Area (initially hidden).
Persistent Status Bar: A bar at the bottom will provide constant system status, just like in GEMINI.
Consistent Spacing: Use padding and margins to create visual "breathing room" between all components.
2. Color & Contrast (The "Floyd-Glass" Theme)
Background: A deep, true #000000 black.
Main Panels (Header, Viewport, Status Bar): These will be "frosted glass" panels. We'll achieve this with a semi-transparent pink background (#FF007F with low opacity, approximated in terminals as a muted pink like #4A0025 or #5A0025) and a prominent, bright pink border (#FF007F).
Text:
Primary Text: High-contrast #FFFFFF (white) for excellent readability against the dark panels.
Header Art: The PRISM_ART text will be a bright #FF007F (hot pink) to stand out against the muted panel.
